_:r18b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "record:priority-live-auction-2009" .
_:r18b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r18b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r18b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Supporting documentation is described at evidence-live-auction-2009 and includes 2008 Sotheby's correspondence and the public catalogue lot. Recommended framing: the artist's asserted conceptual designation of an auction engagement. Avoided claims: 'first in history', publicly witnessed live creation, or precedence over any later artist or event, absent independent recognition and separately published evidence." .
_:r18b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r18b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r18b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The phrase 'made explicit over time' can now be given its earliest located date. On 2013-09-12 the studio principal set the designation down in writing to a university art museum, naming the Sotheby's lot and calling the consignment a performance act of Metaconceptual Art. That letter is the earliest dated articulation of this claim the studio has produced; it is the artist's own declaration, and it postdates the 2009 engagement by four years." .
_:r18b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r18b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
