_:r9b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "record:evidence-live-auction-2009" .
_:r9b2 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355> .
_:r9b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E42_Identifier> .
_:r9b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Evidence status: mixed. Independently verifiable: (1) the public Sotheby's catalogue lot (sale N08533, lot 16) at https://www.sothebys.com/en/auctions/ecatalogue/2009/photographs-n08533/lot.16.html ; (2) two Sun and Rain Works public posts carrying the 'WTF is Art' theme, both still live on the account when checked on 2026-09-10. The earlier reads '#WTF is #Art ?!?!?!' and is displayed by the platform as posted on Aug 28, 2013. It is recorded from a screenshot of that display, and its post identifier has not yet been recorded, so its date is reported as the platform shows it rather than decoded; a displayed date is rendered in the viewer's timezone. The later reads '#WTF is #Art ?!' (X post 373257603108704256). Its timestamp-encoded identifier decodes to 2013-08-30T01:35:22Z, and the platform's own embed gives August 30, 2013. The texts differ, and a post displayed as Aug 28 in any timezone was made no later than 2013-08-29T12:00Z, at least thirteen hours before the second, so these are two posts, not one. Neither is assigned a local day here: nothing in this collection places the studio in a particular timezone in 2013. An earlier version of this passage dated the second post to 2013-08-29 by taking Hawaii-Aleutian time as the studio's local time; that assumption is withdrawn. Recording the first post's identifier would fix its time the way the second's is fixed. Held privately by the studio: the 2008-2009 correspondence, receipts, and photographs. Selected private items can be promoted to public evidence as redaction and rights review are completed." .
_:r9b3 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r9b3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r9b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "The consignment engagement is corroborated by inbound 2008 correspondence from Sotheby's Photographs (confirming intake logistics and naming the department administrator) and by a shared Hana, HI mailing address linking the consignor to the Sun & Rain Works domain receipts. Contemporaneous conceptual intent is evidenced by art-referential documentation (an Andy Warhol volume juxtaposed with the photograph in images sent to Sotheby's). Each item is scoped to what it shows: these evidence identity, consignment, intent, and the concept's public continuity — not a witnessed live-creation event, and not precedence over any later artist or event." .
_:r9b4 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r9b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r9b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P190_has_symbolic_content> "Part of the documentation described here has since been dated and published as a record in its own right. The art-referential documentation photographs — including the frame composing the print with a volume of Warhol's philosophy — carry camera-written Exif placing them on 2008-08-08, and their close-up of the print's verso agrees in four particulars with the public Sotheby's catalogue entry for lot 16. That material is no longer only studio-reported: see the documentation-photograph evidence record." .
_:r9b5 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416> .
_:r9b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
_:r9b6 <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P14_carried_out_by> <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/sun-and-rain-works> .
